<title>UK: Capita shares climb on upbeat press report.</title>
<headline>Capita shares climb on upbeat press report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in outsourcing services company Capita Group Plc rose on Monday following upbeat comments in the Sunday Times on the company's growth prospects, traders said.</p>
<p>Capita shares were up 15p at 400p by 0840 GMT in a generally firm market.</p>
<p>A report in The Sunday Times said Capita had built a strong business since its launch in 1984. It cited new contracts which had not been reflected in the company's results as a potential source of growth and recommended a &quot;buy&quot; on the stock.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom, +44 171 542 8712</p>
